Design: the worker resolves the provider ONCE per job from job.context, before
IncrementalArtifactWriter exists, so an unroutable job fails with an actionable
EngineProviderError and leaves no <stem>.part.wav. EngineProviders is frozen
(dict -> MappingProxyType) and switching profiles builds a new set, so a running
job keeps its engine (covered by a mid-job provider-swap test). Cancel reaches
the engine provider OUTSIDE _active_lock (a Qwen cancel can block on the host),
and a provider exception raised while _is_aborted() settles the job as
cancelled, never failed. QwenEngineProvider gives every segment its own
protocol job id (<worker job>:<n>) because the host settles an id per terminal,
maps zh -> Chinese via language_model_name, and remembers a cancel that lands
before the first segment.
